WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.698
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.698 --> 00:00:10.328
&gt;&gt; Exceptional leaders,
the ones who come to mind

00:00:10.328 --> 00:00:15.138
when you think about people you
admire is that they are known for

00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:19.513
continuing their development
throughout their lives.

00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:24.267
Folks who take a growth mindset
see the challenges they're

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:29.402
facing as something that they
could develop enough to achieve or

00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:33.870
overcome or master or learn from,
so that a failure from

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:39.340
a growth mindset perspective
is an opportunity to learn.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.910
The typical approach is to be judgmental,

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.350
to think of what's happening
as somehow inevitable and

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.520
then to worry about assigning blame for
all those things that are going wrong.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.156
If we can develop more
of a growth mindset,

00:00:55.156 --> 00:00:58.940
we can do a much better job
of creating in ourselves,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.756
a set of capabilities that can
make us more successful precisely,

00:01:03.756 --> 00:01:07.465
because we've run in to
difficulties in the past.

00:01:07.465 --> 00:01:12.446
So at all levels, exceptional leadership
for you as an individual, for

00:01:12.446 --> 00:01:16.947
the organization of the people you
touch there and for the world.

00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:21.849
All have to do with whether or
not you take a developmental approach, or

00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:23.577
a judgmental approach.

00:01:23.577 --> 00:01:29.380
How do your actions as a leader
affect the growth mindset of others?

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.450
What can you do to make it, so

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:36.440
that your workplace is more
developmental and less judgmental?

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.106
&gt;&gt; Transform your Approach to
Leadership Excellence and Development.

00:01:41.106 --> 00:01:44.466
Learn more about SEP,
the Stanford Executive Program.

00:01:44.466 --> 00:01:54.434
[MUSIC]

